 the 1862 spells coelestis where the 1962 spells caelestis: orthography. The stored target read fortitiidine, u read as ii; the page prints fortitudine. The 1962 conclusion is the short Per Dominum., not the written-out form the earlier lane recorded.","relationship":"editorial-projection-exact-to-target","source_date":"2026-10-01 project editorial projection; antecedent Pustet Ratisbon 1862","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.s-ioannae-franciscae-fremiot-chantal-viduae-collect","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","remove stress accents","expand printed ae/oe ligatures to ae/oe","normalise consonantal i to the calendar's j orthography","apply the target printing's punctuation","carry the target's conclusion at its printed length"],"verification_locator":"printed p. 632, no. 3420, marked P; artifact PDF p. 713, right column, under 'Die 21 augusti, S. Ioannae Franciscae Fremiot de Chantal Vid.'","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.temporal-s-ioannae-franciscae-fremiot-chantal-viduae-orations"},"publication":{"basis":"public-domain","evidence":"The wording is preexisting material of the 1962 typical edition under 17 U.S.C. 103(b), which gives a revised edition no exclusive right in material it did not contribute. The independent registered public-domain witness is the tracked 1862 Pustet text artifact and its registered facsimile PDF, read on a page image. The position is settled for the repository at src/sources/inventories/missale-romanum-1962-facsimile-rights-v1.toml, which requires exactly this pairing of 103(b) with a public-domain witness.","locator":"Pustet Ratisbon 1862, Die xxi (August), S. Joannae Franciscae Fremiot de Chantal, Viduae, Oratio, printed p. 524; text-layer lines 72310-72324; read on the page image of the registered facsimile PDF at p. 610; artifact rights_status public-domain on a book first publi